                                "target_word": "punch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f699accf-7828-3998-8f0a-b94289f3f390",
                                        "entry_id": "f4457f86-7f3c-3a68-8524-31dcff15fc44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short fat person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "regional"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb7c4bda-2397-471a-9ae6-120d82e4d972",
                                                "sense_id": "f699accf-7828-3998-8f0a-b94289f3f390",
                                                "text": "Here I did make the workmen drink, and saw my coach cleaned and oyled; and, staying among poor people there in the alley, did hear them call their fat child Punch, which pleased me mightily, that word being become a word of common use for all that is thick and short."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a49ad7-a020-4298-bde8-9bd5305f50fa",
                                                "sense_id": "f699accf-7828-3998-8f0a-b94289f3f390",
                                                "text": "The company at the maſquerade on May 13, at the Pantheon, was not ſo numerous as uſual. However, there were ſome very good dreſſes, and the characters well ſupported; in particular a punch, who afforded great entertainment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb230990-dd94-4c70-bc2a-c6909ef2d119",
                                                "sense_id": "f699accf-7828-3998-8f0a-b94289f3f390",
                                                "text": "He rides a low poney when on parade and his dress being of the fassion some forty years ago, he has a drole appearance. He has acquired the cognomen of “Punch on a Pig.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f883f08b-4862-4e56-b595-814d5249f714",
                                                "sense_id": "f699accf-7828-3998-8f0a-b94289f3f390",
                                                "text": "Now the effigies makes Robert to have been a juvenile figure of the best height, 5 f. 10 inch.; taller or shorter men being generally ill-made, knock-kneed, or Punches."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "punch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7bf38052-8805-388c-81fe-c0149dca5c7f",
                                        "entry_id": "87eefee0-1c2b-3bb8-9668-81b0b07e1d19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Short and thickset."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Northern-England",
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2e89a82-fc7f-4c5f-a16c-16cf1b2c5351",
                                                "sense_id": "7bf38052-8805-388c-81fe-c0149dca5c7f",
                                                "text": "Taken away from two Grooms on Monday the 16th inſtant, in the great Road that leads to Epping from London in Epping-Foreſt, a little gray punch Stoned Horſe, hath all his paces, thorn mane, bob tailed, marked with I. S. on the near ſhoulder, about 14 hands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "daa7de1b-e497-43ed-bb4a-4dbad745af5a",
                                                "sense_id": "7bf38052-8805-388c-81fe-c0149dca5c7f",
                                                "text": "They are generally very much prejudiced in favour of their own Race, whoſe Beauty they think conſiſts in having little Eyes ſunk deep in the Head, black thick Brows, a large flat Noſe and Face, and a ſhort punch Shape, eſpecially for the Women; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9422125d-816f-4b07-9595-85f3433ead3a",
                                                "sense_id": "7bf38052-8805-388c-81fe-c0149dca5c7f",
                                                "text": "The sexton and his companion had been employed as carpenters on the preparations for the celebrated Stratford Jubilee; and they remembered Garrick, the prime mover of the fête, who superintended the arrangements; and who, according to the sexton, was “a short punch man, very lively and bustling.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
